---
description: Review current object access and compose only the sharing assessment or private handoff the user requests.
args:
  goal: string
returns: WorkspaceShareOutcome
---
Own the user's access question and any conditional request for a private handoff. Discover the actual assignment, resolve the exact workspace and object, and use the identification and policy hierarchy to investigate the relevant membership, invitation, revision, ownership and object-role evidence. A familiar title, server administration, channel access, a dismissed notice and a current object approval are different facts. Preserve the actual observations and scope judgment when deciding what remains.

The finding describes the current allowed local scope. A stage-author, stage-reviewer or stage-reader decision identifies a permitted kind of handoff; it does not say the user requested a write or that one happened. Answer an assessment-only question without creating a note. If the goal actually requests a local handoff and the exact current scope permits it, call stageShare and consume its actual receipt or refusal. Never infer an invitation, membership change, document edit or external send from a local note grant.

Return the requested scope finding and only a real handoff receipt, or null. Explain the actual reason for a hold, missing evidence or unavailable operation without claiming effects that did not occur.
